// A `@compileFor` gate is one conjunction, by ruling (KR-281 decision 2): `,` is its AND, `!` negates, and there is no
// `||`. Until 0.9.969 this was a bare "unexpected OROR"; the refusal now names what answers each need, a family flag
// (`DARWIN`), `!`, or a flag the manifest declares. One gate stays one search, and the cover one configuration a gate.
@compileFor(OS_MACOS || OS_IOS)
fn int32 apple() { return 1; }
fn uint8 main() { return 0; }
